	roundMap.set("AA.Qen00076",",AA.Qen00076,Ed-U-Games tm,20070822,12,EvPoMi LoHiBa,Hi16 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,GePa GeFa HiMaBa HiWa MiBa,war;battle;american revolution,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Fl.BritishFlag1776.GE.jpg King George;}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Fl.USFlag1776.GE.jpg Colonialists;,aPRA1_173 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,Answer questions about the American Revolution.,,Rows=7 Cols=1 FntSize=12 FntColor=black BkGndColor=white LnCnt=5 SingleScreen=No Sort=Yes ,AnswerType=MultipleImages Answers=}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Fl.BritishFlag1776.GE.jpg King George;}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Fl.USFlag1776.GE.jpg Colonialists;,Who won the battle of Guilford Courthouse in North Carolina?;March 15: 1781 - Forces under General Cornwallis suffer heavy losses in the Battle of Guilford Courthouse in North Carolina. As a result: Cornwallis abandons plans to conquer the Carolinas and retreats to Wilmington: then begins a campaign to conquer Virginia with an army of 7500 men.;Colonialists,Who won the Battle of Saratoga?;On 7 October 7 1777 - The Battle of Saratoga results in the first major American victory of the Revolutionary War as General Horatio Gates and General Benedict Arnold defeat General Burgoyne: inflicting 600 British casualties with American losses at 150.;Colonialists,Who lost the Battle of White Plains?;October 28: 1776 - After evacuating his main forces from Manhattan: Washington's army suffers heavy casualties in the Battle of White Plains from General Howe's forces. Washington then retreats westward.;Colonialists,Who lost the Battle of Fort Lee?;November: 1776 The Americans lose Fort Lee in New Jersey to General Cornwallis. Washington abandons the New York area and moves his forces further westward toward the Delaware River. Cornwallis now pursues him.;Colonialists,Who won the Battle of Harlem Heights?;September 16: 1776 - After evacuating New York City: Washington's army repulses a British attack during the Battle of Harlem Heights in upper Manhattan. Several days later: fire engulfs New York City and destroys over 300 buildings.;Colonialists,Who lost the Battle of Springfield?;June 23: 1780 - American forces defeat the British in the Battle of Springfield: New Jersey.;British,Who lost the Battle of Princeton?;January 3: 1777 - A second victory for Washington as his troops defeat the British at Princeton and drive them back toward New Brunswick. Washington then establishes winter quarters at Morristown: New Jersey.;British,Who won the Battle of Brandywine Creek?;On 9 September 9 1777 - In the Battle of Brandywine Creek: General Washington and the main American Army of 10:500 men are driven back toward Philadelphia by General Howe's British troops. Both sides suffer heavy losses.;British,Who won the Battle of Fort Lee?;November: 1776 The Americans lose Fort Lee in New Jersey to General Cornwallis. Washington abandons the New York area and moves his forces further westward toward the Delaware River. Cornwallis now pursues him.;British,Who won the Battle of Long Island?;August 27 29: 1776 - General Howe leads 15:000 soldiers against Washington's army in the Battle of Long Island. Washington: outnumbered two to one: suffers a severe defeat as his army is outflanked and scatters. The Americans retreat to Brooklyn Heights: facing possible capture by the British or even total surrender.;British,,,");
